From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:29:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] restore PlayerSpawnLocationEvent in the configuration phase

org.spigotmc.event.player.PlayerSpawnLocationEvent is dead API on this fork:
PrepareSpawnTask.Preparing#tick is the only place that ever constructs it, and
Folia short-circuited that block with a literal `false`. A plugin cannot move a
player's spawn before they join, which is the entire point of the event.

The block is disabled, not unsupported. Everything it needs is still present and
still used by the platform itself - Ready#createPlayer reads back the very
Connection#savedPlayerForLegacyEvents instance this block creates, and constructs
a ServerPlayer on the same thread a moment later if it does not find one.

That thread is the global region thread: RegionizedServer#tick calls
tickConnections, which ticks the configuration listener, which ticks this task.
It is a tick thread, so CraftServer#isPrimaryThread - TickThread.isTickThread on
this platform - is true here exactly as it is on Paper's main thread.

Paper's newer AsyncPlayerSpawnLocationEvent is untouched: its block still runs
afterwards and still starts from this one's result, which is Paper's ordering.

Kill switch: event-config.spawn-location-event=false.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java
index 854f8954ccfd8c34c9f9c91fd1805260f9b429b5..e78fe44bb1befb4e84a7064cbba5f4b0f813a2a1 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/config/PrepareSpawnTask.java
@@ -240,7 +240,22 @@ public class PrepareSpawnTask implements ConfigurationTask {
             Vec3 spawnPosition = this.spawnPosition.join();
             if (this.chunkLoadFuture == null) {
                 // Paper start - PlayerSpawnLocationEvent
-                if (false && this.eventFuture == null && org.spigotmc.event.player.PlayerSpawnLocationEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0) { // Folia - region threading
+                // Lecithin start - restore PlayerSpawnLocationEvent
+                // Folia short-circuited this block with a literal `false`, which makes
+                // org.spigotmc.event.player.PlayerSpawnLocationEvent dead API on this fork: the only
+                // site that ever constructs it is here. The plumbing it needs is all still present and
+                // still used - Ready#createPlayer reads back the very
+                // Connection#savedPlayerForLegacyEvents instance this block creates - so the block is
+                // disabled, not unsupported.
+                //
+                // It is fired from PrepareSpawnTask#tick, which RegionizedServer#tickConnections drives
+                // on the global region thread. That is a tick thread, so CraftServer#isPrimaryThread is
+                // true here exactly as it is on Paper's main thread, and constructing a ServerPlayer on
+                // it is what the platform's own createPlayer already does a moment later on the same
+                // thread. The AsyncPlayerSpawnLocationEvent block below still runs afterwards and still
+                // sees this block's result, which is Paper's ordering.
+                if (fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.EventConfig.spawnLocationEvent && this.eventFuture == null && org.spigotmc.event.player.PlayerSpawnLocationEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length != 0) { // Folia - region threading // Lecithin - restore PlayerSpawnLocationEvent
+                // Lecithin end - restore PlayerSpawnLocationEvent
                     ServerPlayer player;
                     if (PrepareSpawnTask.this.listener.connection.savedPlayerForLegacyEvents != null) {
                         player = PrepareSpawnTask.this.listener.connection.savedPlayerForLegacyEvents;
